{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-logistics-route-019-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/Logistics/RouteCreationFormattersTests.cs", "line": 101, "method": "FormatRejectMessage_AllEnumValuesProduceNonEmptyText", "category": "T3", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "effort": "S", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Logistics/RouteCreationFormatters.cs:272; make any existing case return string.Empty -> red; deleting a case falls to the default at :305 which returns a non-empty string -> stays green", "what_it_asserts": "Every RouteAnalysisStatus except Eligible yields a non-empty reject message.", "why_weak": "The switch default at RouteCreationFormatters.cs:305 returns \"Route source is not eligible (<status>).\", so a status with no dedicated branch still produces non-empty text and the test passes; the comment claims it catches exactly that regression.", "proposed_action": "Also assert the message does NOT start with the default fallback text for each status (or assert per-status distinct copy), so a missing branch reds.", "july_ref": "none"}
